      "learned": "Students confirmed that the fuzzy patches on the ugali and chapati were fungal mould colonies that grew from airborne spores which landed on uncovered, warm and moist food overnight; that bacteria and viruses also cause disease through specific transmission routes; that covering food, refrigerating it or drying it prevents spoilage by removing conditions microorganisms need to grow; and that microorganisms also play beneficial roles in Kenyan food production, agriculture and medicine.",
