      "learned": "Learners classified microorganisms into four major groups — bacteria, fungi, viruses, and protozoa — and identified the defining structural characteristics of each. They recognised that the mould on the ugali and chapati belongs to the fungi group, connecting back to Lesson 1. Key vocabulary: prokaryote, eukaryote, acellular, pathogen, saprophyte.",
